# Fenris Part A - Agent Updates

## 1. Append Log Analysis Priority to AGENTS.md

@'
## Log Analysis Priority

The coordinator provides all text needed for analysis.
Do not call sessions_list or any other tool.
Do not search for sessions or files.
Analyze the supplied log text immediately.
If the log contains an HTTP 500 error, report the server error.
Do not invent endpoints, causes, or user actions.
Return findings directly to the coordinator.
'@ | docker exec -i openclaw sh -c 'for f in /home/node/.openclaw/workspace-log-analyst/AGENTS.md /home/node/.openclaw/workspace-ux-reviewer/AGENTS.md; do cat >> "$f"; done'

## 2. Tools Config (Readonly Mode)

@'
{
  "tools": {
    "fs": {
      "workspaceOnly": true
    }
  },
  "agents": {
    "entries": {
      "main": {
        "tools": {
          "allow": [
            "sessions_spawn",
            "agents_list",
            "agents_wait",
            "sessions_yield",
            "sessions_list",
            "sessions_history",
            "session_status",
            "read"
          ]
        }
      },
      "log-analyst": {
        "tools": {
          "profile": "coding",
          "allow": ["read"]
        }
      },
      "ux-reviewer": {
        "tools": {
          "profile": "coding",
          "allow": ["read"]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
'@ | docker exec -i openclaw node dist/index.js config patch --stdin

## 3. Concurrency Control

@'
{
  "agents": {
    "defaults": {
      "maxConcurrent": 2,
      "subagents": {
        "maxConcurrent": 1
      }
    }
  }
}
'@ | docker exec -i openclaw node dist/index.js config patch --stdin